sw, editeng: sentence case breaks after every full stop

Format > Text > Sentence case walks the selection sentence by
sentence and finds each sentence with the ICU break iterator. Three
faults made it differ from Word (Ely R21.7a):

- ICU's rule SB8 keeps a full stop, spaces and a lower case letter in
  one sentence, so "hELLO wORLD. aNOTHER oNE" was one sentence and
  came out "Hello world. another one". Sentences are now found on a
  copy of the text with every code point mapped to its simple upper
  case; the mapping is one code point for one and keeps a code
  point's UTF-16 width, so every offset stays the same, and ß and
  ligatures keep their form. Words are still found on the original.
- The next sentence started at the word after the last sentence's
  end, so a sentence right after "。" lost its first word. It now
  starts there when a word begins at that end.
- Each later sentence ran to its own end, past the selection, and
  the edit engine clipped every paragraph to the selection's first
  and last indexes. Both now clip to the selection in the paragraph.

Both implementations change alike: Writer's text node and the edit
engine (text boxes, shapes, Impress and Calc text).

